<!-- SECURITY -->
<section class="vx-section" aria-labelledby="security-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Security Design</div>
    <h2 id="security-title">Defense in depth</h2>
    <p>vexes is a security tool that scans untrusted code and metadata. Every layer is hardened against the data it processes.</p>
    <ul class="vx-security-list" role="list">
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Zero dependencies</strong> — the dependency chain is the attack surface. Acorn is vendored. SQLite is Node.js built-in. Nothing to compromise.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Terminal injection protection</strong> — all external data is sanitized. CSI sequences, OSC (BEL and ST), DCS/APC/PM/SOS, C1 control codes, and bare ESC bytes are stripped.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Command injection prevention</strong> — guard uses <code>execFileSync</code> with no shell and an allowlist of known package managers. Fix commands are shell-escaped before display.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Gzip bomb + SSRF protection</strong> — tarball downloads enforce streaming size limits, HTTPS-only URLs, and a registry host allowlist.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Never recommends vulnerable fixes</strong> — every suggested version is cross-checked against OSV before presenting it to the user.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Prototype pollution protection</strong> — config file merging rejects <code>__proto__</code>, <code>constructor</code>, and <code>prototype</code> keys.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
